# methylphosphonic_acid.msf
# Methylphosphonic acid (methanephosphonic acid)
# pKa1=2.380 (first P-OH, q=0→-1)
# pKa2=7.740 (second P-OH, q=-1→-2)
# Source: Perrin 1981
# Simplest organic phosphonate — fills the gap between inorganic H3PO4
# (training) and biological phosphate esters. The P-C bond instead of
# P-O bond changes the electron density on P significantly.
# pKa2=7.74 is the only organic P-acid in the physiological pH range.

